    "body": "- [ ] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [ ] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n\r\nThere is a line of document says:\"    -- Basic mappings (better 'jk', save with Ctrl+S, ...)\"\r\nBut I didn't find the mapping of \"better jk\" so I added it.\r\nI'm not a native English speaker so I'm sorry if my words are confusing.\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2023-03-23T18:26:25Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nBy \"better 'jk'\" it meant that `j` and `k` [move by visible lines when no `[count]` is set](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/9f8b92998a9964e03535c2c7e0708958e23e261a/doc/mini-basics.txt#L233-L234).\r\n\r\nThis type of Insert mode exit introduces delay when typing `j` and/or `k` in Insert mode. Which is not good. A [\"better-escape\"](https://github.com/max397574/better-escape.nvim) approach is planned for this (see #86), just not as separate module but as a function in 'mini.misc'. So, sorry, I'll close this.",
            "created_at": "2023-03-23T18:26:25Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/279#issuecomment-1481697435",
